2026-10-04T18:58:16.4327644Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-04T18:58:16.4337815Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-04T18:58:16.4338348Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-04T18:58:16.4339044Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-04T18:58:16.4339405Z 
2026-10-04T18:58:16.4339688Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-04T18:58:16.4340087Z 
2026-10-04T18:58:16.4340413Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-04T18:58:16.4341361Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-04T18:58:16.4341901Z 
2026-10-04T18:58:16.4342122Z If you would like to
2026-10-04T18:58:16.4342717Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-04T18:58:16.4343027Z 
2026-10-04T18:58:16.4343217Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-04T18:58:16.4343570Z   $ sh ./install-nix
